  "id": "drug-tolerance",
  "term": "drug tolerance",
  "definition": "Drug tolerance is a reduced response to a drug after it has been used repeatedly, so larger amounts are needed to produce the same effect that a smaller amount once did. It can result from changes in how the body processes the drug or from cellular, physiological, or behavioral adaptation to its effects.",
